  "description": {
    "main": "An anthology on love edited by Ingo Niermann, the ninth Solution volume from Sternberg Press. Contributors range from Etel Adnan to Paul B. Preciado, in manifestos and speculative fiction.",
    "extended": "<p>An anthology on love edited by Ingo Niermann, the ninth volume of Sternberg Press's Solution series.</p><p class=\"mt-6\">Where earlier volumes took up geopolitical questions, this one treats love through biopolitical and psychosexual lenses. Contributions range from manifestos to speculative fiction and consider love as a mix of charity, sex, trust, lust, economics, genetics and cybernetics, with embodiment and identity understood as fluid systems with permeable boundaries. The book has 188 pages and 18 black-and-white illustrations.</p><p class=\"mt-6\">Contributors include Etel Adnan, Douglas Coupland, Eva Illouz, Ben Marcus, Chus Martínez, Momus, Paul B. Preciado and Emily Segal, alongside Niermann himself. The publisher lists the volume as out of print.</p>"
  },
